From workstream 05, for workstream 04 to integrate (shared core).

- submit keeps which credential let a request in (general or a sender's
  token, with its version); when the request's turn in the Citizen's
  lane comes, and again in beforeSend right before the bytes leave, that
  credential must still be current, or it is refused BadCapability and
  nothing is sent (closes the window 0006's lane opened between
  authentication and sending).
- revoke-capability with source 'any' removes the general token (its
  version moves on).
- NFT transfer: workstream 04's resident check refuses a still-valid
  token's send before anything is built (SessionNotDelegated with
  ResidentHolderChanged, or ResidentUnverified when the holder cannot be
  read); tested here with stub chain and holder reads.

Test agent-wallet-revoke-transfer (no key made, derived or used,
nothing signed; run under workstream 05's no-keys guard): 3 pass; with
citizen-lane, sender-capability, run-facts: 13 pass.
